==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} {{term|déifier}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|deificare|deificāre}}, from {{term|deus||god}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈdeɪɪfaɪ/|/ˈdiːɪfaɪ/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈdiː.ə.faɪ/|/ˈdeɪ.ə.faɪ/}}
* {{audio|en-us-deify.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en-us-deify-2.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|deif|i|ed}}

# {{transitive}} To make a [[god]] of (something or someone).
# {{transitive}} To treat as [[worthy]] of worship; to regard as a [[deity]].

====Synonyms====
* {{italbrac|to make a god of something}}: [[apotheosize]], [[exalt]], [[idealize]]

